## TokenLighten MCP (compact)

Tools: `tl_read_file`, `tl_edit_file`, `tl_search_files`; use for all workspace read/search/edit; shell for build/tests/git. First lookup: `tl_read_file {"cwd":"<workspace>","query":"<entire user request, verbatim>","task":{"epoch":"new"}}`; unknown path omit `targets`. Use native tools if requested, TL is unavailable/bypassed, or its result is unusable or scope incomplete/absent; return to TL when usable. CSS/literals: `action:"find"` (references: language symbols only).
Each call: top-level `cwd` (no pwd; else `cwd-required-for-edit`); add no `cwd` to a `next`. In parallel: one fixed `lane` from call 1. Same request: latest `task.id` exactly→`task.handle`; never `epoch:"new"`. User-declared read-only=`task.profile:"answer"`, change=`"generic"`; otherwise omit.
Unknown `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report; no edit/field inference. Follow `decision.kind`; `act.answer`/`act.edit` ends discovery. `decision.next[]`: all calls in one tool-call turn, verbatim; refusal→`retry` only. Trace branch/loop guards and arg identities; names, definitions, logging ≠ execution. `evidence[].body` is exact source; use it without rereading. If required body is missing after `act.answer`, read that target. Batch independent reads. Later reads=`targets:[{path|handle,range}]`, no `query`; docs=`select.sections`. `next` whole call, verbatim; hints advisory. Lost context: same call with `task.force_serve:true`. `read.receipt`: follow `next`; else act or stop. `edit_rules` in a reply: follow them.
